/*
 * remotix-niente-spegnimento.rules — the first of the three belts of
 * `DECISIONI.md` §4.7: "nobody switches the server off".
 *
 * Installed in /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/.  Number 50 and not 49: it must win
 * over v1's (`49-remotix-niente-spegnimento.rules`), which covered three
 * actions out of twelve — see below.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ⛔⛔ WHY `power-off`, `reboot` AND `halt` ARE NOT ENOUGH — [M] 15 August 2026
 *
 * v1's rule listed those three.  ⛔ But logind, when the machine has
 * sessions of SEVERAL USERS, does not ask for `power-off`: it asks for
 * `power-off-multiple-sessions`.  ⇒ v1's rule failed **exactly in the
 * case it had been written for** — the machine with others connected — and nobody
 * would have seen it, because with a single user it works.
 *
 * ⚠ And `*-ignore-inhibit` is the third form: it is what is asked of whoever
 *   switches off OVERRIDING an inhibition — that is overriding ours, the one that
 *   keeps the session up (`SessionManager.Inhibit`, §2.2 of phase 5).
 *
 * `[M]` The twelve actions were read from
 * `/usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.freedesktop.login1.policy` on the test
 * machine.  ⛔ `org.freedesktop.login1.halt` does NOT exist on this systemd: v1's
 * rule had a dead line.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ⭐ ROOT NEEDS NO EXCEPTION, and it was MEASURED
 *
 * `[M]` 15 August 2026, from the test machine with this rule in force:
 *
 *     from nicfio (ssh)   CanPowerOff = "no"
 *     from root           CanPowerOff = "yes"
 *
 * ⛔ Because logind, before asking polkit, looks at the **capabilities** of whoever
 *    asks: whoever has `CAP_SYS_BOOT` — that is root — is authorised and polkit is
 *    not consulted at all.  ⇒ `sudo systemctl poweroff` keeps
 *    working **without this rule providing for anything**, and the maintenance
 *    of the machine stays as it always was.
 *
 * ⚠ And the consequence that really bites lies elsewhere: **checking this
 *   rule CANNOT be done from the server**, which runs as root and would always be
 *   answered "yes".  It must be done from the CHILD, after it has become
 *   the user.  A check made from the wrong place is a check that always
 *   says yes.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * ⚠ `polkit.Result.NO`, NEVER `AUTH_ADMIN`
 *
 * `"challenge"` **shows** the entry in the menu instead of removing it — it holds on GNOME
 * (`gnome.md` §5.1) and on KDE (`kde.md` §1579).  An entry that appears and asks for
 * a password is worse than an entry that is not there: it promises something.
 */
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
    var vietate = [
        "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off-multiple-sessions",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.power-off-ignore-inhibit",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.reboot",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.reboot-multiple-sessions",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.reboot-ignore-inhibit",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.suspend",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.suspend-multiple-sessions",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.suspend-ignore-inhibit",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.hibernate",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.hibernate-multiple-sessions",
        "org.freedesktop.login1.hibernate-ignore-inhibit"
    ];

    for (var i = 0; i < vietate.length; i++)
        if (action.id == vietate[i])
            return polkit.Result.NO;
});
